From 56507111f52c49647443a09f5a9403e11e4e5c6d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 09:42:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Q08-YIELD-1: log what a q08 run read and spent, learn the
 source floor from it, stop repeat-class repairs (q08-signal-engine 0.29.0)

Root cause: 266 of 311 q08 runs in the 7 days to 2026-10-19 ended gate_failed (17 ok,
q08_gate_pass_rate_7d 0.06, 83,598 neurons per published piece). engine_runs recorded the
outcome but not the size of the source material the writer saw or how many model calls the
run spent, so nobody could say which failures came from sources too thin to ground 2800
characters. The only thin-source test was a flat 600 characters of fetched article
(THIN_MIN_ARTICLE). On the repair path, every short prune after an earlier round had already
pruned the same classes of unsupported claim spent a model revision plus a two-family
re-verification: 19 failed runs in 7 days extended a pruned draft in round 2 or later, 11 of
them wrote the extension and still failed, 494 s on average.

Measured (q08-signal D1 10fd74b7, 2026-10-19 09:20Z to 10:05Z):
- 7 days: 311 runs, 266 gate_failed, 17 ok, 14 deferred, 14 skipped; ok per day 7,4,1,3,1,1,0.
- failed: 184 carry unsupported claim, 95 too short after pruning, 12 tick budget spent.
- source size was logged nowhere, and the nearest proxy does not separate the outcomes
  (signal_log.friction_point: hn published avg 1587 chars over 9 rows vs gate_failed 2234 over
  192; arxiv published 1455 over 8 vs gate_failed 1409 over 58). A constant would be a guess,
  so the floor is derived from the log going forward instead.

Change (q08-signal-engine/worker.js, mirror identical):
1. engine_runs gains nullable source_chars, source_kind, compose_calls, verify_calls through
   the worker's own bootstrap (pragma_table_info guard, one ALTER per missing column); every
   generation insert (skipped, gate_failed, ok, essay and forecast) goes through insertRun,
   which falls back to the old column list if the bootstrap or the insert fails, so logging can
   never cost a run its row. Model calls are counted on a per-run copy of env (compose-side
   calls as compose_calls, fact-check and reader-panel calls as verify_calls); the meter
   restarts after each row so a failed forecast and the essay in one tick count their own calls.
2. Source-sufficiency pre-gate: once five ok runs of the last 30 days carry a logged
   source_chars, a thin candidate must reach the thinnest source that has published (never
   above the 2200 rich-source threshold). Below it the run ends skipped with no model call, and
   the measured candidates are marked thin_skipped in signal_log, which the existing 24-hour
   retry window reads: they are retried after 24 hours and the next tick moves on to other
   candidates (nothing is dropped, and the same top candidates are not re-measured every tick).
   Before five logged ok runs, or when the floor cannot be read, the flat 600-character test
   applies unchanged. The unreadable-article refusal marks its candidates the same way.
3. Repair loop: the first prune round that leaves the draft under the 2800-character floor
   while its flagged claim classes were already flagged by an earlier round stops the repair
   and records "stopped: repeat <class> after a prune left the draft below the floor" in the
   trail. The first short prune still gets its one extension (PRUNE-EXTEND-1 unchanged).
Not changed: PUBLISH_MIN_CHARS 2800, the FACTS and fabrication rules, every fact-check
threshold, the final read, the rich-source threshold.

Migration migrations/2026-10-19-q08-gate-yield-metrics.sql (APPLY-BY ci): control_registry rows
for the pre-gate (filter, replace, applied, alternate = the flat test, 24-hour retry) and the
repair stop (guard, keep), failure_modes q08-thin-source-composed and
q08-repeat-class-extension with hourly d1-query@q08-signal detector contracts, and a
capability_ledger row. No delete, no backup table needed.

Tests: q08-signal-engine/source-sufficiency.test.mjs (42 assertions): floor derivation,
verdicts, schema bootstrap on a legacy table, insert binding, ALTER refusal fallback, generate()
with stubbed fetch (skipped before any model call, source_chars/source_kind/compose_calls 0
recorded, thin_skipped marks, next tick composes from another candidate, flat test before five
logged runs, unreadable article), repair stop on a recurring class, first short prune still
extended, PUBLISH_MIN_CHARS 2800. Against the base worker the repair assertions fail (the
extension was composed: lengthRevision true, composeCalls 1) and the rest of the suite cannot
run (the helpers do not exist). verify.test.mjs keeps its thinOk pin; all q08 suites pass.

Closing probes after deploy: /health version >= 0.29.0; engine_runs rows with
compose_calls NOT NULL appear and carry source_chars; the issue probes of 99929 and 99930
(q08_gate_pass_rate_7d >= 0.5, q08_neurons_per_published_piece_7d <= 6000) stay open until the
metrics converge; the two fm- detector contracts read 0.

Issues: D1 agent_issues 99929 and 99930 (METRIC-TRIGGER-537 and 538) and 2606 (Q08-PUBLISH-STALL-AUTO-1); these are
qnfo-audit ids, not GitHub numbers, and all three stay open until their probes pass.

