he 2800-character floor, the one model revision extends that pruned draft from the source (every surviving sentence kept, the deleted claims named as not to be restated) instead of rewriting the unpruned draft, and the result is re-verified in full. 0.28.0 EXTERNAL-PROPERTIES-1 (owner 2026-10-14: '"By property" SHALL ALSO INCLUDE Q08.ORG AND READING.Q08.ORG'): every tick ends by mirroring the finished runs of the last 7 days (published or rejected at the gate, title and stage only) into qnfo-audit.content_external_items, so fleet.qnfo.org/content shows q08.org by property. 0.27.0 (owner 2026-10-14: "REJECTION RATES ARE UNACCEPTABLY HIGH ... WHY ZERO PUBLISHED TODAY?"; engine_runs 394-417: 2 of 24 published, 13 of 16 failed essays stopped on a flagged lede claim): Q08-LEDE-PRUNE-2 (a flagged lede sentence is cut when another lede sentence remains; ledeProblems still guards the opening) and Q08-GROUND-PROVENANCE-1 (the fact-check ground states the item's title and the site it appeared on as sentences, and the reviewers are told the source line is source material; "the paper appears on arxiv.org" was flagged unsupported in runs 415 and 417). 0.26.1 Q08-TITLE-REPAIR-2: every attempted title repair leaves a q08_reader_tests trail note (the reply opening or the error; runs 405 and 406 left none), and a title wrapped in a preamble, a Title: label or a code fence is read. 0.26.0 Q08-TITLE-REPAIR-1 (agent_issues 2284, 2503): a writer draft whose only writer-gate problems are its title gets one short title call to the same writer before the next writer is tried (8 of 15 nemotron drafts in a day were refused for the title alone while nemotron wrote every published piece). // 0.25.1 WORKERS-BP-LOGGING-1 (#2342): swallowed catches log; Q08-PANEL-METRIC-STATE-1 (#1895): the panel effective-votes and panel-unavailable writes set state MEASURED. // 0.25.0 Q08-ENTITY-BACKGROUND-1: the products, projects and organisations a headline names get their own full Wikipedia article in the background, so the system the analysis explains is in the checked source (run 390). 0.24.2 was: // 0.24.2 Q08-PRUNE-BODY-FLOOR-1 + Q08-SOURCE-CONCESSION-1: the prune floor is the publish floor measured on the body, and a fact-check item whose reason concedes it is in the source material (FAQ, comments, background) is dropped (run 388). 0.24.1 was: // 0.24.1 Q08-PARAPHRASE-ITEMS-1: in the reporting, a fact-check item whose reason concedes the content (phrasing, not explicitly stated, implied) and whose sentence has no digit, quotation or name does not fail the essay (run 387). 0.24.0 was: // 0.24.0 Q08-BUDGET-ROUTE-1: while the workers-ai or total ai_spend cap is breached the writer order puts nemotron and gpt-oss before kimi-k2.6 (BUDGET-SOFT-ROUTE-1, issue 1780). 0.23.2 was: // 0.23.2 CRON-ONLY-HEARTBEAT-1 (agent_issues 2397, pillar autonomy): each hourly scheduled run ends with a qnfo-audit fleet_heartbeat upsert (ok=0 when generation threw); write errors are logged. // 0.23.1 Q08-NAME-COMPOUND-1 + Q08-COMPOSE-TRAIL-1 (each writer's gate result is kept in q08_reader_tests): in a hyphenated compound only the capitalised parts are checked as names ("AI-driven", "Claude-generated"; run 386). 0.23.0 0.23.0 Q08-TECH-SYSTEMS-1: the analysis explains the technical system (components, data flow, the design decision or constraint behind the event, the trade-off) instead of an incentive template; the background reads full Wikipedia articles on the technologies; both reader prompts judge technical understanding. 0.22.1 0.22.1 Q08-PRUNE-FLOOR-2: the prune floor is the publish floor (3000 characters with title and verdict), so the repair stops instead of eroding a draft that can no longer publish (run 385). 0.22.0 0.22.0 Q08-WRITER-UPGRADE-1: kimi-k2.6 writes first with thinking off, nemotron and gpt-oss as per-request fallback. 0.21.0 0.21.0 Q08-FINAL-READ-1 + Q08-SOURCE-DEPTH-1 (eight comments and arXiv abstracts up to 3000 characters; the fact-checkers count background and comments as source): the exact text that would be published needs 2800 characters of body and a final two-family reader panel (vacuity-focused prompt, mean 4, no judge under 3, fails closed) after the fact check and its prunes. 0.20.3 0.20.3 Q08-ANALYSIS-CONCRETE-1: an analysis-check item counts only when the sentence it quotes has a digit, a quotation or a name; abstract reasoning flagged against the reviewers' own instruction is dropped (run 383). 0.20.2 0.20.2 Q08-VERDICT-NORM-1: near-miss verdict lines are normalised, and a first draft whose only problem is the verdict line gets the verdict micro-call (which now reads the essay) before a full rewrite (run 382). 0.20.1 0.20.1 Q08-MARK-SHIFT-1: an analysis marker placed where the guard rails refuse it moves later, paragraph by paragraph, to the first accepted place instead of sending the whole essay to the strict check (run 381). 0.20.0 0.20.0 Q08-ANALYSIS-DEPTH-1: an essay publishes only with a systems analysis of at least two paragraphs and 700 characters whose opening refers to something the piece said (a thin one goes to the one model revision); the inference prune keeps the analysis section (Q08-ANALYSIS-KEEP-1), and a "This <noun>" sentence left after a cut goes with it (Q08-DANGLING-CUT-1). 0.19.3 0.19.3 Q08-SOURCE-ORDER-1: Hacker News stories and arXiv papers are tried before GitHub repositories (alternating, never the last source twice); a repository is used only when no story or paper ahead of it has enough source material (runs 354, 356, 358, 375, 379: repository essays had no system to analyse). // 0.19.2 Q08-ANALYSIS-AUTO-1 (run 378): when the writer leaves the <!-- analysis --> marker out, the analysis starts at the first body paragraph after the lede and context written in reasoning language (same 60% and 600-character guard rails, still checked for invented facts); the run error records the analysis split (marked, auto, none). // 0.19.1 Q08-SOURCE-GROUND-1 (run 377): the fact-check ground carries the source description the writer is given (kind, title, link, site) and labels each part (discussion comments, linked article, background), so "posted on apple.com" and "a commenter on Hacker News said" can be verified instead of failing as not in source. // 0.19.0 Q08-ANALYSIS-SECTION-1 (owner 2026-10-13: big-picture systems analysis): the writer marks where its systems analysis starts with an invisible <!-- analysis --> line; the reporting before it keeps the sentence-by-sentence fact-check, the analysis after it is checked only for concrete invented facts (events, named parties acting, dates, numbers, quotations, studies), the deterministic name/year/figure check still covers the whole text, the analysis may be at most 60% of the body, and the marker never reaches readers or the published page. // 0.18.2 (run 375): "README", "CHANGELOG", "GitHub" and "repository" are not names the grounding check needs in the source (the source of a repository piece is its README); the fact revision is told to keep a news lede naming the subject and where it appeared. // 0.18.1 Q08-LEDE-PRUNE-1: the fact-check prune never deletes sentences of the first paragraph (a piece was published opening "Users therefore trust ..." after its lede was pruned); a flagged claim in the lede sends the draft to the model revision, and every pruned draft is re-checked with ledeProblems. // 0.18.0 Q08-CONTEXT-1 (owner 2026-10-13: "totally lacking in context and big-picture systems analysis"): each essay gets a BACKGROUND pack of verified reference text (Wikipedia lead sections for the story's subject and recent news coverage) that the writer may cite and the fact-check verifies against; the directive requires a context section and a systems analysis (parties, incentives, constraints, feedback loop, who gains and who pays, where else it operates); the fact-check treats framed analysis that adds no new name, number or event as not a violation, and a reviewer reason calling an item analysis marks it reasoning; readers cap a piece that only retells its source at 3. // 0.17.6 Q08-PRUNE-VERDICT-1 (run 369): the sentence prune sets the verdict line aside and puts it back unchanged, so a verdict that shared a paragraph with the last sentence is no longer damaged into a "missing verdict" failure. // 0.17.5 Q08-LEDE-SPLIT-1 (run 368): an overlong first paragraph is split at a sentence boundary into a lede of at most 70 words and a following paragraph, instead of failing "lede too long"; nothing is added or removed. // 0.17.4 Q08-TICK-BUDGET-1 (agent_issues 2479): an essay after a failed forecast waits for the next tick when more than 240 s are used (run 366 left no row: forecast 256 s + essay up to 644 s reached the 15-minute limit), repair rounds stop at a tick deadline, and every early exit of generate() writes an engine_runs row (skipped or deferred) instead of vanishing. // 0.17.3 Q08-LEDE-1 (fleet audit 2026-10-13): forecasts open with a news lede too (the case they start from, where it was reported, the forecast and its probability) and are checked by ledeProblems; the forecast register is plain explanatory journalism, not the earlier detached register; the site description and home page say what q08 is in plain words. // 0.17.2 PUBLISH-STALL-DIGEST-1 (fleet audit 2026-10-13): the stall issue is rewritten on every stalled tick with the hours, a 24 h breakdown of the stage each run ended at and the newest errors, and turns critical after 24 h; stall failures are logged instead of swallowed. // 0.17.1 Q08-FULLTEXT-1 (agent_issues 2470): the richest thin candidate is written from only when its full text was fetched (at least 600 characters); an abstract-only candidate is skipped with a reported reason. // 0.17.0 Q08-LEDE-1 (owner 2026-10-13): inverted-pyramid essays. The writer is told the source (kind, title, link) and must open with a news lede (who did what, where it appeared, when, why it matters) before the analysis; a deterministic lede check (names the subject,