ddresses and @cf/ model ids untouched). Q08-EDITOR-TITLE-CARRY-1 (run 343): an editor draft whose title is missing, over 100 characters or a label title keeps the writer's passing title instead of failing the gate; the body stays the editor's. // 0.14.3 Q08-EDITOR-ROUND-2 + Q08-FACT-OBJECT-ITEM-1 + Q08-FACT-SHAPE-1 (runs 338-341): an unlabelled fact-check item whose quoted text has no digit, quotation or capitalised name and uses causal or modal wording, with a reason that quotes nothing and names no date, figure or name, is reasoning (deleted when the draft can spare it, never a failure); a close panel miss (mean at least 3 of 5) after the editor gets one more editor pass that applies the readers' named cuts, read by a third panel; a fact-check item returned as an object is rebuilt as "LABEL: claim -- reason" instead of "[object Object]". // 0.14.2 Q08-FACT-INFERENCE-2 (run 338): reviewers skipped the FACT/INFERENCE label and wrote 'inference from source' in the reason; an unlabelled item whose reason names an inference, interpretation, generalisation, assumption or paraphrase (and no name, date, number or quotation) is an INFERENCE; the prompt shows an example answer. // 0.14.1 Q08-EDITOR-VERDICT-CARRY-1 (run 337): an editor draft that dropped the final 'worth your time' line gets the writer's line back instead of failing the gate. // 0.14.0 Q08-STALL-RETRY-1 (agent_issues 2286): while no piece has been published for 2 hours, the :30 cron makes a second generation attempt after its audit (same gates and caps, never overlapping the :00 attempt; ops_config q08_stall_retry = off stops it). // 0.13.2 Q08-FACT-INFERENCE-1 (agent_issues 2286): the fact-check labels each finding FACT or INFERENCE; only FACT findings fail a draft (unlabelled ones count as FACT), INFERENCE findings are deleted when the draft can spare them; runs 333-335 failed only because reviewers listed the essay's own reasoning next to real fact errors. // 0.13.0 FRAMING-REPAIR-1 + FACTCHECK-DEGRADE-1 (agent_issues 2284, 2286, 2288; pillar reach): a gate failure made only of phrase-level tells is repaired without a model call (the flagged sentences removed, full gate re-run, at most a quarter of the sentences; logged as framing_repair rows and in the run error), the writer, editor and forecaster prompts carry one line naming the framing idioms the gate rejects, the retry feedback shows each flagged phrase in its sentence, and the fact-check panel tries every non-writer family on Workers AI (the writer families join the pool, cheaper sibling first) before a draft fails as unavailable. // 0.12.0 Q08-EDGE-CACHE-1 (issue 2343, pillar reach): plain GET pages are served from the edge cache for their public max-age=300 (TTFB 0.8-1.6 s measured: every view rendered from D1); a cache hit on a piece page still counts both reads; every HTML response carries Referrer-Policy and Permissions-Policy. // 0.11.19 Q08-READER-NOTHINK-1 (issue 2085): reader judges use the measured per-model reasoning switches and a 6000-token budget (2000 left reasoning judges without a verdict on 11 panel reads in 3 days). // 0.11.18 Q08-EDIT-FLOOR-1: the editor pass applies the readers' cuts and is held to 1800 characters, not the 2800-character writing floor (runs 319, 323, 327: readers asked to delete restating paragraphs, the editor was told to keep 2800 characters, the second panel rejected the same padding); forecasts keep the writing floor. // 0.11.17 Q08-PRUNE-FLOOR-1: a draft repaired by deleting the reviewers' quoted sentences is held to a 1500-character floor (the audit-repair floor), not the 2800-character writing floor, so the repair stops falling back to a model revision that writes new unsupported detail (runs 292-332: no piece since 2026-10-10 06:05); five prune rounds, one model revision at most, and the repair trail is kept in the run error. // 0.11.16 SINGLE-LETTER-1: a single capital letter (the O of O(n), a variable, a list label) is never read as a name by the grounding check 